{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"affluent-conveyable-dromedary","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`infra/scripts/observability.sh` §4/§4c/§4d/§4e all count journal markers CUMULATIVELY —\ngrep the whole journal for a token, publish `total - prev`, where `prev` is a stored\noffset file. Each guards the negative case identically:\n\n    new=$((total - prev))\n    [ \"$new\" -lt 0 ] && new=$total\n\nA negative delta only happens when the journal LOSES history it previously had —\njournald vacuuming by `SystemMaxUse`/`MaxRetentionSec`, a `journalctl --vacuum-*`, or\nthe persistent journal being cleared. In exactly that case the guard republishes the\nENTIRE remaining count as \"new this interval\", re-counting markers that were already\ncounted and already alarmed on.\n\n## Why it matters most for `review_interrupts`\n\n`rebar-autodeploy-review-interrupts` (monitoring_autodeploy.tf) is\n`period=900, evaluation_periods=1, datapoints_to_alarm=1, threshold>0` — deliberately a\nsingle datapoint, because the `signal-unavailable` case must not wait an hour to surface.\nThat sensitivity means ONE spurious republish pages, and it pages with a reason field\nthat points an investigator at `journalctl` history that has just been deleted.\n\nThe same shape affects `voter_errors`, `review_bot_merge_change_errors`, and\n`deploy_errors`, but those have multi-datapoint cadences, so the blast radius is smaller.\n\n## NOT currently firing — this is latent, not the cause of anything observed\n\nMeasured on i-00880b2c7f13527c5 on 2026-08-12 while diagnosing\n[rebar:7b4a-0f39-1a45-4ce9]: journal total = 7, offset file\n`/var/lib/rebar/autodeploy-interrupt-offset` = 7, and the `rebar-autodeploy.service`\njournal still reaches back to 2026-07-03T19:50:40Z. Every CloudWatch datapoint matched a\ndistinct journal line. So no rotation has occurred on this box yet and no observed alarm\nfiring is explained by this. It is filed because the hazard was ruled OUT by measurement\nrather than by design, and the next `--vacuum` or a `SystemMaxUse` trip would expose it.\n\n## Suggested direction (not prescriptive)\n\nThe clamp is trying to be safe and picks the least safe of the three options. Either\n`new=0` on a negative delta (treat lost history as already-counted — under-counts at most\none interval), or make the count time-windowed (`journalctl --since` the last run) so it\nis not cumulative at all and no offset file is needed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A shrinking journal no longer republishes already-counted markers as new.\n- [ ] A test covers the negative-delta path for at least the `review_interrupts` counter.\n- [ ] The chosen behaviour on lost history is stated with its rationale in the script.","id":"2dc7-31b7-ecbb-4cd2","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"observability marker counters re-count on journal rotation, spuriously re-firing the 1-datapoint review-interrupts alarm"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786516847414574001,"uuid":"816a49ce-2bb0-41de-9671-2fa48dbf11e4"}